== Functional Levels of a Digital Computer

+ Electronic devices and circuits (transistors, logic gates) - hardware
+ Functional units (ALU, memory, interfaces) - firmware (microprogramming) and hardware
+ Physical machine, interconnection structures, and peripheral devices - hardware
+ Operating system kernel - BIOS - firmware
+ Operating system and its API - software
+ Programming language and compiler - software
+ Applications and software libraries - software
+ User interface - software

== Hardware vs. Software

- Some functions can be implemented in either hardware or software
- The decision to implement a function in hardware or software is based on:
  - Implementation cost
  - Execution speed
  - Cost/performance ratio
  - Operational reliability
  - Frequency of change
- The current trend is to move more functions into hardware